# RTK (Rust Token Killer)

Prefer RTK-wrapped shell commands so CLI output stays compact in context.

When executing CLI commands, use the `rtk` prefix:

- `git status` / `diff` / `log` / `add` / `commit` / `push` / `pull` → `rtk git ...`
- `cat` / `head` / `tail` / file reads via shell → `rtk read ...`
- `grep` / `rg` → `rtk grep ...` or `rtk rg ...`
- `ls` / `find` → `rtk ls ...` / `rtk find ...`
- `gh ...` → `rtk gh ...`
- test runners (`pytest`, `cargo test`, `npm test`, etc.) → `rtk test ...` or `rtk cargo ...` / `rtk jest ...` as appropriate
- When in doubt, prefix the CLI command with `rtk`

Do not invent RTK subcommands. If unsure whether RTK supports a tool, run the plain command.
